\details{
For each medium epoch (default 15 minutes), a long window (default 60
minutes) is evaluated per axis.  An axis is scored as non-wear when both
its standard deviation is below \code{sd_threshold} and its range is below
\code{range_threshold}.  The non-wear score is the number of axes (0--3) that
meet both criteria, and an epoch is non-wear when the score is at least
\code{wear_threshold}.  An epoch is clipped when more than \code{clipping_threshold}
of its samples on any axis exceed \code{clip_threshold} (or, if any sample
exceeds \code{1.5 * clip_threshold}, the whole epoch is clipped).  Short wear
bouts surrounded by long non-wear bouts are then relabelled as non-wear,
following GGIR part 2.

GGIR reads files in chunks (24 hours for GT3X files) and scores each chunk
separately.  With \code{approach = "2023"}, a window that starts in one chunk
cannot label epochs in the next, so GGIR's \code{nonwearscore} can be lower for
the first epochs after a chunk boundary.  This function scores the whole
recording at once.  GGIR also imputes time gaps before scoring; this
function does not.
}
